# --- Blog posts moved from root-level /<slug> to /blog/<slug> ---------------
# The blog used to publish posts at the site root. They now live under /blog/.
# Preserve every old post URL with a 301 to its new home.
/30-years-of-cybercafes               /blog/30-years-of-cybercafes               301
/centos-vs-ubuntu                     /blog/centos-vs-ubuntu                     301
/essential-versus-accidental-complexity  /blog/essential-versus-accidental-complexity  301
/gmail-is-20                          /blog/gmail-is-20                          301
/mythical-man-month-50                /blog/mythical-man-month-50                301
/php-is-30                            /blog/php-is-30                            301
/rebranding-javascript                /blog/rebranding-javascript                301
/rethinking-rest                      /blog/rethinking-rest                      301
/rfcs                                 /blog/rfcs                                 301
/software-attributes                  /blog/software-attributes                  301
/the-quality-without-a-name           /blog/the-quality-without-a-name           301

# Note: the old /hello-world blog post is NOT redirected — /hello-world is now
# the site's about page (see /about below). The post itself lives at
# /blog/hello-world.

# --- Historical slug changes (carried forward) ------------------------------
# "rebranding-rest" was renamed to "rethinking-rest" long ago.
/rebranding-rest                      /blog/rethinking-rest                      301
/blog/rebranding-rest                 /blog/rethinking-rest                      301

# --- Site pages -------------------------------------------------------------
/about                                /hello-world                               301
/contact                              /                                          301

# --- Catch-all --------------------------------------------------------------
# Show 404 for unmatching routes.
/*                                    /404.html                                  404
